==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*süü}}, from {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*süji}} or {{m|urj-pro|*süxi}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|süü}}, {{cog|kpv|си}}. The abstract meaning is specific to Baltic-Finnic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[syː]}}
* {{rhymes|yː|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|syy|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[fibre]]
# [[filament]]
# [[grain]] {{gloss|linear texture of a material or surface}}; used in plural ('''''syyt''''')
#: ''Koivun '''syyt''' ovat yleensä suorat.''
#:: The '''grain''' of birch is usually straight.
# [[reason]]
#: '''''Syy''' tähän on...''
#:: The '''reason''' for this is...
#: ''On '''syytä''' tietää, että...''
#:: It is '''worth''' knowing that... (literally: There is a '''reason''' to know that...)
# [[fault]]
#: ''Se on sinun '''syytäsi'''.''
#:: It is your '''fault'''.

